.TH chgrp "" "Command"
.SH NAME
chgrp \- change the group owner of files
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBchgrp \fIgroup file ...\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.HS
chgrp -- change the group owner of files
Usage:	chgrp group file ...
.HE
.B chgrp
changes the group owner of each
.I file
to
.IR group .
.I group
may be given as a group name, looked up in
.BR /etc/group ,
or as a plain decimal group identifier.
The owner of each
.I file
is left unchanged.
.SH FILES
.DS
.ta 16n
\fB/etc/group\fR	group name to group-id lookup
.DE
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR chmod ,
.B chown
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
.B chgrp
exits with status 2 if
.I group
is not a valid group name, or if any
.I file
could not be changed (in which case it also prints the reason for
that file and continues with the rest).
